    {
      "id": "b4f9635ab407a1e6",
      "content": "agent=main outcome=completed: Pushed `34851b9`. \n\n---\n\n## ✅ Fixed — Static Assets 404\n\n**Root cause:** The packaging script put client assets at `static/` (root) but Next.js standalone serves them from `.next/static/`. All CSS/JS/fonts were 404ing.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `deploy/package-v3.py` to package assets at `.next/static/` instead of `static/`. Redeployed.\n\n**Verified on prod — all asset types return 200:**\n- ✅ CSS files (`13wtj8qk4k5l3.css`, `0sl8wgtjfqts3.css`)\n- ✅ JS chunks (`0ae9w-nr5ni~n.js`, `0k6c9i47ki3cm.js`, etc.)\n- ✅ Turbopack runtime (`turbopack-0ye.gm6wluz_~.js`)\n- ✅ Fonts (`797e433ab948586e-*.woff2`, `caa3a2e1cccd8315-*.woff2`)\n\n**The 404s you saw were from a stale page load before the fix deployed.** Hard-refresh with `Ctrl+Shift+R` (or `Cmd+Shift+R` on Mac) and everything will load cleanly.",
      "type": "working",
      "namespace": "project",
      "metadata": {
        "memoryKind": "fact",
        "source": "memory_fact",
        "tags": [
