      "id": "3bae5e705341bc72",
      "content": "[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file C:\\\\Users\\\\hyper\\\\workspace\\\\HyperNexus\\\\HANDOFF.md, lines 1-70\\n1: # HANDOFF — OpenCode Extension Max Surface + Full Verification (v1.0.15)\\n2: \\n3: ## Status: COMPLETE \u0026 VERIFIED (2026-10-19, two sessions)\\n4: Branch: feat/mimo-plugin-max-surface. Kernel: bin/hypernexus.exe **v1.0.14** (built session 1). Plugin: **v1.1.0 / manifest 1.0.15**.\\n5: \\n6: ## Session 2 (v1.0.15) — lifecycle + graph capture + hot-path optimization\\n7: ### COMPLETE TEST MATRIX: 269/269 ALL GREEN\\n8: 1. OpenCode plugin battery: **115/115** (was 109; +memory lifecycle +file-observation kernel round-trip)\\n9: 2. MCP tools battery: **23/23** · 3. MCP sweep: **46/46** · 4. Core without extension: **18/18**\\n10: 5. MiMo extension battery: **51/51** · 6. MiMo TUI battery: **16/16**\\n11: \\n12: ### Session-2 changes\\n13: - `hypernexus_memory_delete` (id delete + tag fan-out) — full memory lifecycle\\n14: - `/hn-restore` — handoff pickup (completes HANDOFF workflow)\\n15: - Structured `file-change:*`/`file-read:*` observations with filesModified/filesRead → kernel knowledge graph\\n16: - Assistant-turn advertiser feed (throttled per role)\\n17: - FIXED: `/hn-purge` sent `{tag}` but `/api/agent-memory/delete` reads `{id}` (was inert); context-hook assistant feed used undefined `sessionID`\\n18: - OPTIMIZED: hot-path context injection parallelized (FTS harvest ∥ suggestion fetch); negative caching skips all network attempts while kernel known-down\\n19: - Live-verified in real OpenCode session: hooks fire (audit trail `src=opencode-plugin`), hot-reload picked up new tool mid-session (84→85 tools in merged namespace)\\n20: \\n21: ## Session 1 (v1.0.14) — full V2 plugin + kernel router parity\\n22: ### COMPLETE TEST MATRIX (session 1): 196/196 ALL GREEN\\n23: 1. OpenCode plugin battery (`bin/test-opencode-ext.mjs`): **109/109** — registration surface, 28 tools live-kernel, 10 commands, 3 skills, MCP registration, worktree strategy, every hook, V1 shim, kernel-down degradation contract\\n24: 2. MCP tools battery (`bin/test-mcp-tools.mjs`): **23/23**\\n25: 3. MCP sweep (`bin/test-mcp-sweep.mjs`): **46/46** — every registry tool invoked with schema-derived safe args + stdio transport (initialize / tools/list=58 / tools/call). 6 destructive/external tools documented-skipped\\n26: 4. Core WITHOUT extension (`bin/test-core-noext.mjs`): **18/18**\\n27: \\n28: ## What was delivered\\n29: ### 1. OpenCode V2 plugin — `addons/opencode/` (THE deliverable)\\n30: - `plugin/hypernexus/index.js` — V2 `setup(ctx)` + V1 `server()` shim in one package\\n31: - 28 tools (namespace `hypernexus`): memory store/search/fts/vector/list, scratchpad, context_harvest, record_observation, tool_search/tool_discover/suggest_tools, mcp_status/servers/tools/search/call, session_search/context/handoff, skill_search/manage, code_search, knowledge_graph, billing_status, audit_log, subagent\\n32: - 10 commands: /hn-status /hn-store /hn-remember /hn-search /hn-tools /hn-session /hn-context /hn-plan /hn-summary /hn-purge (report commands → `session.synthetic`, context commands → `session.prompt`)\\n33: - 3 skills (hypernexus, hypernexus-ops, hypernexus-workflows) registered programmatically AND materialized as SKILL.md\\n34: - Hooks: session prompt (offset-safe `@memory:key` expansion + suggestion feed + session priming w/ active goal), context (≤400ms FTS status+recall+suggestions block), compaction (preserve pointers), model.request (identity headers), retry (observability), tool execute.before/after (RBAC + audit + auto-store), permission.evaluate (HYPERNEXUS_RBAC=audit|ask|deny), shell create.before (env injection), event stream (turn-end observation)\\n35: - MCP: auto-registers `hypernexus mcp` stdio server via `ctx.mcp.transform` (respects existing config; `codemode` option; startup timeout 45s)\\n36: - Worktree strategy (HyperNexus-managed, `.hypernexus-worktree.json` linkage)\\n37: - `plugin/hypernexus/rpc.js` — shared RPC contract (TOOL/COMMAND/CAPABILITY/KERNEL/BUDGET)\\n38: - `instaâ€¦",
