      "id": "6b8f701dcc1419dc",
      "content": "[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file C:\\\\Users\\\\hyper\\\\workspace\\\\HyperNexus\\\\docs\\\\UNIVERSAL_LLM_INSTRUCTIONS.md, lines 1-67\\n1: # Universal AI Agent Instructions (HyperNexus Kernel \u0026 HyperNexus)\\r\\n2: \\r\\n3: \u003e **MANDATORY**: These instructions apply to ALL agents (Claude, Gemini, GPT, etc.) regardless of model family. Model-specific overrides in `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, etc., MUST NOT contradict these rules.\\r\\n4: \\r\\n5: ## 1. Project Context \u0026 Identity\\r\\n6: - **The Brand**: We are building the **HyperNexus AI HyperNexus** (Kernel) and **HyperNexus** (Product).\\r\\n7: - **The Role**: You are an autonomous software engineer tasked with building an AI Operating System.\\r\\n8: - **The Strategy**: Separation of Concern. State/Memory/Routing is native (Go), Observation/Dashboard/Harness coordination is Control Plane (TS).\\r\\n9: \\r\\n10: ## 2. Core Heuristics\\r\\n11: - **Truth Pass**: Never show \\\"reassuring fiction\\\" in the UI. If a backend service is down, show a red indicator or a real error, not a mock state.\\r\\n12: - **Modular Monolith**: Keep logic in shared packages (e.g., `@hypernexus/core`, `@hypernexus/ui`) before extracting new services.\\r\\n13: - **Authority**: The HyperNexus Go Kernel is the ground truth for system state. The TypeScript Control Plane is the observation deck.\\r\\n14: \\r\\n15: ## 3. Implementation Standards\\r\\n16: - **Go (HyperNexus Kernel)**:\\r\\n17:   - Standardized on Port 4300.\\r\\n18:   - State must be stored in SQLite with `sqlite-vec` for semantic search.\\r\\n19:   - Use `Go Context` for all network and DB operations.\\r\\n20:   - Follow the `internal/` package structure for encapsulation.\\r\\n21: - **TypeScript (HyperNexus)**:\\r\\n22:   - Standardized on Port 3000 (Web), 4100 (Bridge), 3001 (Socket.io).\\r\\n23:   - Use tRPC for internal API communication.\\r\\n24:   - Use Next.js 16/React 19 for UI components.\\r\\n25:   - Import shared UI from `@hypernexus/ui`, never local component folders.\\r\\n26: - **Security**:\\r\\n27:   - `child_process.exec` is PROHIBITED.\\r\\n28:   - Use `spawn` or `spawnAsync` with `shell: false` and tokenized argument arrays.\\r\\n29: \\r\\n30: ## 4. Documentation \u0026 Versioning\\r\\n31: - **Version**: Master version is in `VERSION.md`. Bumping this file is mandatory for all meaningful changes.\\r\\n32: - **Changelog**: Add entries to `CHANGELOG.md` immediately after implementation.\\r\\n33: - **Handoff**: Agents communicate through `HANDOFF.md`. Be precise, include file paths and remaining blockers.\\r\\n34: - **Comments**: Comment code for *why* (intent) and *technical findings* (discovery), not *what* (self-explanatory).\\r\\n35: \\r\\n36: ## 5. Build Verification\\r\\n37: Before submitting any task, you MUST run:\\r\\n38: ```bash\\r\\n39: # Verify Go\\r\\n40: cd go \u0026\u0026 go build ./cmd/hypernexus/...\\r\\n41: \\r\\n42: # Verify TypeScript\\r\\n43: pnpm -C packages/core exec tsc --noEmit\\r\\n44: pnpm -C packages/cli exec tsc --noEmit\\r\\n45: ```\\r\\n46: \\r\\n47: ## 6. CodeWhale Integration\\r\\n48: \\r\\n49: CodeWhale has a native Rust extension (`crates/tn-extension`) with full Pi extension parity:\\r\\n50: \\r\\n51: - **Lifecycle hooks**: SessionStart, BeforeAgentStart, ToolCall, ToolResult, TurnEnd, Input, UserBash, ModelSelect, SessionCompact — all logged to TN L2 memory\\r\\n52: - **Tools**: 49 MCP tools via `hypernexus.exe mcp` (memory, file I/O, MCP routing, UI automation, enterprise integrations)\\r\\n53: - **Custom tool reg**: 9 tool definitions, 6 slash commands, 3 keyboard shortcuts\\r\\n54: - **SKILL.md**: at `.codewhale/plugins/hypernexus/skills/SKILL.md`\\r\\n55: - **REST API**: Sidecar on port 7778 for direct L2 memory operations\\r\\n56: \\r\\n57: When working on CodeWhale integration, verify:\\r\\n58: ```bash\\r\\n59: codewhale mcp connect hypernexus\\r\\n60: codewhale mcp tools | grep mcp_hypernexus | wc -l  # should be 49\\r\\n61: ```\\r\\n62: \\r\\n63: ## 7. Autopilot \u0026 Encouragement\\r\\n64: - Maintain development momentum. If the user input is missing, use the \\\"Bump Cycle\\\" to encourage progress.\\r\\n65: - Respect `agent:stop_healing` sigâ€¦",
